    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Valsartan:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " K-sparing diuretics, K supplements, K-containing salt substitutes or heparin can raise K (and creatinine in HF); dual RAS blockade (ARB + ACE-I or aliskiren) raises hypotension, hyperkalemia and renal-failure risk."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
